cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below and credit the sources: Tracés ferroviaires : Train Nomade (https://trainnomade.fr), d'après © les contributeurs OpenStreetMap et les horaires SNCF Voyageurs (ODbL)."
type: dataset
title: "Railway track geometry between consecutive stops in France (GeoJSON and GTFS shapes)"
abstract: >-
  Track geometry of every passenger railway section between two consecutive stops of the SNCF timetables
  (about 3,200 sections), routed on OpenStreetMap tracks, with length, maximum speed, bridges, tunnels and
  electrification, as CSV, simplified GeoJSON (WGS84) and a GTFS shapes.txt keyed by UIC codes. Recomputed
  every month by Train Nomade. Live files: https://api.trainnomade.fr/donnees/v1/traces-ferroviaires.csv,
  https://api.trainnomade.fr/donnees/v1/traces-ferroviaires.geojson and
  https://api.trainnomade.fr/donnees/v1/traces-ferroviaires-shapes.txt
authors:
  - name: "Train Nomade"
    email: contact@trainnomade.fr
    website: "https://trainnomade.fr"
version: "2026-10-25"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
license: ODbL-1.0
url: "https://trainnomade.fr/donnees/traces-ferroviaires/"
repository: "https://www.data.gouv.fr/organizations/train-nomade/"
keywords:
  - railway
  - track
  - geometry
  - GeoJSON
  - GTFS shapes
  - OpenStreetMap
  - SNCF
  - France
  - open data
references:
  - type: data
    title: "OpenStreetMap"
    authors:
      - name: "OpenStreetMap contributors"
    url: "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"
  - type: data
    title: "Réseau SNCF TGV, Intercités et TER (GTFS)"
    authors:
      - name: "SNCF Voyageurs"
    url: "https://transport.data.gouv.fr/datasets/horaires-sncf"
